                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Ionball 2 had some serious issues with mouse control that affected a lot of users and the developer never addressed it.  So I was skeptical about Ionball 3.\n\nI went ahead and made the purchase, and glad I did.  It's a great game.\n\nArcade mode is pretty much regular breakout except you have some ball control by dragging the mouse in the direction to influence the ball.\n\nStory mode has lots of interesting puzzles to solve along with breakout style play.\n\nI also really like the soundtrack, however it would be better if the music was queued by events rather than just being a repeating playlist. Some of the songs have this \"boss fight\" intensity but it just seems weird when one of those tracks come on mid level.\n\nI could also make the argument this game is too easy. But breakout is a pretty casual game to start with so that is fine.  The game does allow saving your progress in both Story and Arcade mode so you don't have to finish a game in one sitting.\n\nThe visual style is pretty cool too... and most importantly, the mouse control is spot on, so no worries about that.",
